{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-124412-r4514346","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tempe Mendoan I","sourcePageId":124412,"sourceRevision":"4514346","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T02:05:56Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Koavf","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tempe%20Mendoan%20I&oldid=4514346","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:16.807Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Fried recipes","Category:Indonesian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using green onion","Category:Recipes using rice flour","Category:Recipes using soy","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2413ee2771a533cc4abd75ee94969d13553762c13bd4560a2019f7ccff3e67fe","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Fried recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Tempe mendoan fried tempeh.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Indonesia|Cuisine of Indonesia]]\n\n'''Tempe mendoan''' is a dish made from thin tempeh, fried with flour so as to taste deliciously piquant. Traditionally in the Banyumas territory, tempe mendoan was made from thin, wide tempeh, one or two sheets cooked at a time. However, tempe mendoan also could be made from normal tempeh that was sliced very thin but wide.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Rice Flour|rice flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Flour#Wheat Flour|wheat flour]]\n* 2 cloves of [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 1 piece [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallot]], ground\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]], ground\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|white pepper]], ground\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 125 [[Cookbook:mL|ml]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* 2 pieces [[Cookbook:Green onion|green onion]], thinly [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 300 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Tempeh|tempeh]], size 10&times;15 cm\n* ½ ml [[Cookbook:Oil|cooking oil]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Combine rice flour, wheat flour, garlic, shallot, coriander, pepper, salt, water, and green onion to make a thin [[Cookbook:Batter|batter]].\n# Dip each piece of tempeh into the batter, and coat entirely.\n# Warm the oil in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]], and put it on the stove until hot. Put each piece of coated tempeh into hot oil.\n# [[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|Fry]] the tempeh until hardened and well done. Don't wait until it becomes yellow and crispy.\n# Remove the tempeh from the oil, letting the oil drip from the tempeh so that there is not much oil on it.\n# Serve tempeh with [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy bean sauce]] and sliced small [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|chilies]].\n\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using soy]]\n[[Category:Fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n\n[[id:Resep:Tempe Mendoan]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tempe Mendoan I","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"100 g rice flour","s